                <pb facs="0513" n="497" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p1/pg497"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>On June 1, Secretary of State Dean Acheson began his testimony before the Senate
                    Armed Services and Foreign Relations Committees. He testified daily through June
                    9, with the exception of Sunday, June 3; see <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hearings</hi>, pages 1667 ff. On June 2, specifically in reply to questions
                    from Republican Senator H. Alexander Smith of New Jersey, Mr. Acheson stated
                    that a cease-fire and military settlement at or near the 38th parallel in Korea
                    would be acceptable to the United Nations, and that the Chinese Communist
                    authorities would have to be dealt with on these matters; see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ibid</hi>., pages 1782–1783.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
